If package-lock.json is missing, npm will:
1. Read version ranges from package.json (e.g. ^5.2.1)
2. Go online and find the latest version that fits that range
3. Install it (maybe 5.3.0)
4. Generate a new lock file based on what it actually installed
So without the lock file, you lose reproducibility.





